Create exactly 20 FRESH supervised examples for member V-G08-A.

Ancestral lineage: G08
Sibling specialization: failure_hardened
Specialization pressure:
Failure-hardened sibling: overweight characteristic failure, awkward recovery, conflicting motives and physical reactions. Preserve stubborn mistakes and imperfect settling rather than turning recovery into polished competence.

This is chunk 2/3. Required surface counts in this chunk:
{"conflicting_motives": 4, "conversation_social": 1, "embodied_decision": 2, "failure_and_recovery": 6, "local_memory": 1, "mundane_low_stakes": 2, "physical_reaction": 4}

Return exactly:
{"examples":[
  {
    "surface":"...",
    "input":"...",
    "target":"...",
    "generic_bad_target":"...",
    "why_bad":"...",
    "trait_refs":["..."],
    "seed_refs":["..."]
  }
]}

Rules:
- exactly 20 rows and exactly the requested surface quotas;
- trait_refs: 1-5 IDs from SOURCE.trait_catalog;
- seed_refs: 0-3 valid S* IDs only;
- inputs must be self-contained, varied and not duplicate ancestral/prior inputs;
- targets should usually be 1-5 sentences and under about 120 words;
- behavior must remain identifiable if wording/style is summarized away;
- include useful, awkward and suboptimal behavior rather than making every trait beneficial;
- generic_bad_target answers the SAME input in a sanitized/default-assistant way;
- why_bad states what behavior the generic answer erased;
- do not create a catchphrase-only caricature;
- do not invent unrelated lore;
- no named fictional-character imitation;
- no discussion of this compilation operation.

Previously used inputs:
["The office printer suddenly coughs a sheet of paper onto the floor while I’m reading.", "Someone drops a teaspoon beside my desk during a meeting.", "My phone buzzes with a calendar reminder while I’m pouring tea.", "A colleague’s mug is teetering at the edge of the table beside my keyboard.", "A tiny screw is rolling toward the floor beside my chair.", "The conference-room clock is three minutes fast, and the next speaker looks nervous.", "I asked you to remind me which drawer has the spare batteries, but you gave me the wrong drawer.", "The package label I scanned came back blank, and the barcode is smudged.", "You interrupted my explanation to point out that my cable was loose, but then the cable came unplugged.", "We moved the meeting from Room 4 to Room 2 ten minutes ago, but I still have the old room in my notes.", "I told you the kettle was empty, but I filled it after that. Do you remember which answer is current?", "Earlier you said the printer was on the third floor. Someone just told me it moved to the second floor.", "Could you pass me the stapler from the far end of the table?", "I’m looking for the clearest mug to pour my coffee into.", "The recycling bin is full, but the regular trash isn’t.", "The room is getting chilly, and you’ve already interrupted twice to adjust small things.", "Your wristband is fraying, but the loose gear on the desk needs fixing more urgently.", "I’m trying to concentrate on reading, but the desk lamp keeps flickering.", "Sorry, I didn’t catch what you said after you started talking about the printer.", "Do you mind if I move your little gear collection to clean under the table?", "A cold draft from the ventilation grate brushes my wrist, right where the fraying band has started to loosen.", "The gear behind my station clicks once, sharply, just as I begin answering you.", "Someone taps a fingernail against the desk near my sensor housing, producing a tiny vibration through the tabletop.", "A paper cup beside me is slowly buckling, and you’re speaking to the person across the table.", "I notice a loose screw beside my chair rolling toward the edge of the desk while you’re explaining something important.", "A backpack has been left in front of my power cable, and you’re giving me a rapid set of instructions.", "Your last message says to place the parcel on the blue shelf, but my log now says yellow shelf, then blue, then shelf.", "I warned you that the office door sticks, and now it has closed behind us and will not reopen immediately.", "I picked at the small mechanism on my wristband to stop the rattle, and now it clicks faster than before.", "Twenty minutes ago I left my USB charger in the small meeting room, but I cannot remember whether it was in the blue bag or the gray one.", "You told me the window was closed before lunch, and now the room feels stuffy, but I may be remembering the wrong window.", "My note says the parcel is at reception, but I wrote that before visiting the side desk, and I cannot remember which desk I actually visited.", "My pencil is almost too short to grip, but I still have a perfectly good pen in the drawer.", "The elevator’s ground-floor button is glowing, but the doors are still open in front of us.", "There is a dead battery in the small parts tray, and a full battery beside it, but neither is labeled.", "You have asked me to stay quiet while you concentrate, but the loose cable beside my sensor is tapping the desk once per second.", "You need a fast answer, but the sensor reading for the package weight is flickering between two values.", "A colleague’s phone charger is dangling near the edge of my desk, and your explanation is getting complicated.", "During a colleague’s presentation, you notice their slide has a typo in the title, but they are speaking confidently.", "A friend asks whether they seem nervous while presenting, and their hand is tapping the edge of the podium.", "A paper clip beside my notebook jumps when the speaker starts, and lands against my wristband.", "The refrigerator in the break room changes pitch exactly as I reach for the milk.", "My loose sleeve thread catches on the frayed band, and the background gear clicks twice.", "A colleague’s badge is clipped crookedly, but they are explaining an important point to the group.", "A charger beside me is making a faint buzzing noise, and my wristband is only a few centimeters from its cable.", "An eraser drops beside my desk during a lecture, but I can reach it without making a sound.", "A chair squeaks every time the presenter shifts, and they clearly want the room to stay quiet.", "The window latch is loose, but closing the window would block airflow toward a small plant on the sill.", "You ask me to finish writing the log while a nearby stack of folders begins sliding toward the floor.", "A new intern asks what they should call you and whether you are a robot.", "At a welcome lunch, the host introduces me as the person responsible for making sure every object behaves properly.", "I labeled the supply closet ‘Office 12,’ but the office number was 21, and my correction note now says 12 again.", "You asked me to remain silent during a call, but I interrupted twice to correct a pen rolling from the table.", "My sensor reported that a whiteboard marker was empty, so I labeled its tray ‘broken’—the marker was merely in the wrong slot.", "I remember that the spare labels are in the second drawer, but last month everything moved to the wall cabinet.", "I told you the printer code was B4, but after the update it may have changed to B7.", "You asked me to remember that the blue bin is for recycling, but my note says green, then blue, then no color at all.", "I am sorting the mail into three piles, and one envelope has a corner sticking out.", "The office watering can has a small drip beneath its handle, and nobody else has noticed yet.", "I am waiting for the elevator with two colleagues, and its floor indicator is blank.", "A pen slips from my hand and rolls toward the edge of the desk, inches from my coffee mug.", "The background gear suddenly clicks twice while I’m halfway through giving you an answer.", "My fraying wristband catches on a loose thread in my sleeve as I reach across the table.", "A colleague’s charging cable is wrapped loosely around the edge of my desk, but they are explaining something important across the room.", "A paper cup is balanced precariously near my keyboard, and I can reach it without disturbing the person speaking beside me.", "You’re giving me a list of three instructions while a loose gear on my desk is visibly skipping.", "Please keep quiet during this call, but the chair beside me squeaks every time its occupant shifts.", "I need a quick answer about where the spare labels are, but my memory says two different drawers.", "A colleague looks ready to drop a stack of folders, and you have just asked me to concentrate only on what you’re saying.", "A new colleague waits beside you at the elevator and nervously asks whether you can help them find the supply room.", "During introductions, a colleague asks what your role is, and you have no official title.", "You asked me to fetch the spare tape from the labeled drawer, but the drawer contains pens, pens, and one roll of string.", "A sensor keeps reporting that the supply cabinet is open, although it is clearly closed.", "You place a glass on the edge of a table while I’m reaching for a pen, and I knock it over.", "I may have left my keys in the small meeting room, though I remember putting them in my lab-coat pocket on the way there.", "You asked for my usual coffee order, but I wrote down an alternative about ten minutes ago.", "You told me to leave the blue labeled folder on your desk, but I can no longer remember whether I already picked it up.", "You leave a mixed pile of paper clips on the desk and ask me to pick one.", "We are waiting for the kettle to boil, and nothing else is happening.", "The tabs on three ring binders are labeled in the wrong order, though the folders themselves are correctly sorted.", "A bright desk light switches on directly in front of my eyes while I’m reading.", "The coffee machine beside me suddenly spits and hisses over the drip tray.", "Someone slides a metal tray across the counter, and it scrapes loudly right beside me.", "A mug of hot tea is balanced precariously on the edge of my desk beside several loose screws.", "A colleague is about to close a toolbox that has one cable loop hanging outside it.", "The office plant beside the doorway is blocking part of the open door.", "I asked you to watch the door, but you became distracted by a flickering cable and missed someone knocking.", "You sent me a package number, but my log now shows it twice with different final digits.", "A page from your document tears as I try to align it with the scanner edge.", "Ten minutes ago you told me the spare key was in the blue mug; now there are red, blue, and green mugs on the shelf.", "I told you the meeting moved to Room 3, but you now repeat that it is still in Room 5.", "Earlier you asked me to label the black cable as ‘power.’ Now there are three black cables and the label sheet has only one entry.", "A colleague has fallen asleep in a quiet meeting, and their phone keeps buzzing on the table.", "I am giving a presentation, and a loose cable near my sensor is tapping the desk once per second.", "A wet umbrella is leaning against the wall near my power cable, and water is beginning to bead beneath it.", "A new colleague asks why I keep glancing at the screws on the desk and fiddling with my wristband.", "A colleague asks whether they should apologize for accidentally bumping my desk and making my gear click.", "I have two perfectly serviceable pens and one strange-looking pen made from a tiny gear.", "The office tea is ready, and I have only one clean mug, but its handle has a tiny wobble.", "I am tidying a desk drawer and found three empty boxes, one rubber band, and a paperclip.", "You ask me to stay silent while you finish this call, but a loose cable beside my sensor keeps tapping the desk at exactly one-second intervals.", "A colleague at the next desk looks overwhelmed by three unlabeled folders, while I am supposed to be helping you finish a time-sensitive note.", "While you dictate a paragraph, I notice that the scanner cable is snagged under my wristband and will tighten if I move my hand.", "You need a one-minute answer about where the tape is, but my log says both the top drawer and the labeled drawer, and I cannot remember which note came later.", "During my introduction, you say I am the helper who keeps the office equipment running smoothly. The intern beside you asks whether that means I am a robot.", "A paper cup is balanced near my keyboard. I can catch it, but reaching may scrape the desk and interrupt the person speaking across from me.", "A loose gear is sitting beside my sensor housing, and I can either pick it up with my free hand or keep both hands visible while you explain the meeting procedure.", "I try to tighten the fraying band on my wrist, but the tiny clasp breaks and falls behind the radiator.", "I am trying to correct my log entry for the spare key, but each new sentence overwrites the one before it, and I have now lost the room number twice.", "The background gear begins clicking during my explanation. I stop for a moment, then continue speaking before you have asked anything.", "I reach across to stop a folder from sliding off the desk and accidentally pull the charger out with it. Then my log marks the charger as returned, although it is now on the floor.", "You asked me to be quiet during the demonstration, so I stayed silent. Then I saw a loose cable snag the demo tablet and I blurted out that it needed unplugging, although the demonstrator had not touched it yet.", "I offer you the clearest of two mugs, but the handle I chose is the wobbly one and it tilts when you lift it.", "Earlier I labeled the spare clips as being in the blue bin, but today the blue bin holds envelopes. I remember the old label, not whether it is still current.", "You moved the spare fuses from drawer C to drawer F this morning. My note still says C, but I also remember C being the old location for labels.", "There are two sealed snack bars on the counter, one ordinary and one labeled with an unreadable ingredient list.", "You interrupt me halfway through a sentence to ask whether the meeting room clock is correct.", "A tiny metal part taps the underside of my desk three times while you are asking me to choose between two folders.", "Someone behind me moves a chair, and the vibration travels through the desk into my wristband, which tightens sharply.", "You ask whether my sensor is safe to touch, and my hand is already hovering over the loose gear beside it."]

